@startuml SystemTopLevelBehaviour

title RIVUS - System Top Level Behaviour

actor "External Client" as Client
participant "Component Library Manager" as Clm
participant "Component Version Manager" as Cvm
participant "Component Enabler Manager" as Cem
participant "Build System Manager" as Bsm
participant "Engine Version Manager" as Evm
participant "Engine Caching System" as Ecm
participant "Engine Performance Manager" as Epm
participant "Data Input Manager" as DIm
participant "Data IO Manager" as DIom
participant "Data Processing System" as Dpm
participant "Data Output Manager" as Dom
participant "Token Pool Manager" as Tpm
participant "Token Transmission Manager" as Ttm
participant "Logical Execution Timer" as Let
participant "Execution Manager" as Exm
participant "Engine Event Manager" as Eem
participant "Diagnostic Event Manager" as Dem
participant "Diagnostic Logging Manager" as Dlm
participant "Fault Event Manager" as Fem
participant "Failsoft System" as Fsm
participant "Watchdog Manager" as Wdm
participant "Debugger Manager" as Dbm
participant "Engine Runtime" as Runtime

Client -> Clm: Request component composition
Clm -> Cvm: Resolve component versions
Cvm --> Clm: Return compatible versions
Clm -> Cem: Enable selected components
Cem --> Clm: Components enabled
Clm -> Bsm: Load composition configuration
Bsm -> Evm: Validate engine version
Evm --> Bsm: Version accepted
Bsm -> Ecm: Read cached build configuration
Ecm --> Bsm: Return cached configuration
Bsm --> Client: Composition ready


Client -> DIm: Submit input data
DIm -> DIom: Normalize input stream
DIom -> Dpm: Deliver input data
Dpm -> Tpm: Acquire execution token
Tpm -> Ttm: Reserve token transmission
Ttm --> Tpm: Transmission channel ready
Tpm --> Dpm: Execution token granted
Dpm -> Let: Start execution timer
Let -> Exm: Schedule execution unit
Exm -> Runtime: Execute configured composition
Exm -> Epm: Report execution performance
Epm -> Eem: Publish performance metrics
Runtime -> Eem: Publish execution event
Eem -> Dem: Forward diagnostic event
Dem -> Dlm: Record execution diagnostic
Dlm --> Dem: Diagnostic stored
Runtime --> Exm: Return execution result
Exm -> Let: Stop execution timer
Exm -> Dom: Publish output data
Dom -> DIom: Serialize output stream
DIom --> Client: Return output data

Wdm -> Runtime: Check runtime heartbeat
Runtime --> Wdm: Heartbeat status
alt Fault detected
    Runtime -> Fem: Report fault event
    Fem -> Dem: Publish fault diagnostic
    Dem -> Dlm: Log fault context
    Fem -> Fsm: Request failsoft action
    Fsm -> Runtime: Apply degraded operation
    Fsm -> Wdm: Confirm controlled recovery
else No fault detected
    Wdm --> Runtime: Continue operation
end

Client -> Dbm: Request execution trace
Dbm -> Eem: Query execution events
Eem --> Dbm: Return event trace
Dbm --> Client: Return debug information
Client -> Runtime: Stop composition
Runtime -> Ttm: Release token transmission
Ttm -> Tpm: Return execution token
Tpm -> Ecm: Persist runtime state
Ecm --> Runtime: State persisted
Runtime --> Client: Shutdown complete

@enduml
